ocument migration and support policy."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make history integrity a version-independent project fact and prevent self-confirming destructive repairs."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Pinned CI, global CLIs, and external packages agree whether immutable project history is valid before any mutation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"A healthy workspace can be diagnosed as corrupt and repaired into a form that breaks its authoritative CI gate."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"History format capability negotiation and repair preconditions keep every supported CLI version truthful and safe."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"GitHub #1040 provides symmetric evidence that 2026.8.7 and 2026.8.15 disagree on identical bytes; GitHub #1036 retracts merge attribution and points to this root cause."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"Identical tracker bytes read and repaired by pm 2026.8.7 and 2026.8.15"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Validate one committed workspace with both released binaries, repair with the newer binary, then validate the unchanged repaired bytes with both versions."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Supported versions agree, or an older binary returns a typed incompatible-format refusal and cannot repair the stream."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The versions produce mirror-image drift verdicts and each accepts only its own repaired encoding."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-2htk4p","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":